{:edb/db-before-t 757 :edb/db-after-t 758 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534070 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:40:44.833Z" 13194139534070 true] [17592186059473 1100 "Calculate $-2A$, if\n$A=\\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2 & -1 \\ 4 & 7} \\right\\rbrack$." 13194139534070 false] [17592186059473 1100 "Calculate $-2A$, if \n$A=\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2 & -1 \\\n        \t4 & 7\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack.$" 13194139534070 true] [17592186059473 1145 "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-2$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2A &= -2\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\cdot 2 & -2 \\cdot (-1) \\\\ -2 \\cdot 4 & -2 \\cdot 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534070 false] [17592186059473 1145 "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2A & =-2[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\cdot 2 & -2\\cdot (-1) \\\\ -2\\cdot 4 & -2\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534070 true] [17592186059474 1100 "If $k {A} =\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t1 & 3 & 4 \\\n        \t6 & 0 & -2\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack,$\nwhere ${A} =\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2 & 6 & 8 \\\n        \t12 & 0 & -4\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" 13194139534070 true] [17592186059474 1100 "If $k {A} = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {1 & 3 & 4 \\ 6 & 0 & -2} \\right\\rbrack$,\nwhere ${A} = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2 & 6 & 8 \\ 12 & 0 & -4} \\right\\rbrack$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k$." 13194139534070 false] [17592186059474 1145 "To express $kA$, we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nkA &= k \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 12 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2k & 6k & 8k \\\\ 12k & 0 & -4k\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2k & 6k & 8k \\ 12k & 0 & -4k} \\right\\rbrack = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {1 & 3 & 4 \\ 6 & 0 & -2} \\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the top-left elements, $2k$ and $1$. Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2k &= 1 \\\\\nk &= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." 13194139534070 false] [17592186059474 1145 "To express $kA,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 12 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2k & 6k & 8k \\\\ 12k & 0 & -4k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2k & 6k & 8k \\\n        \t12k & 0 & -4k\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack\n=\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t1 & 3 & 4 \\\n        \t6 & 0 & -2\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the top-left elements, $2k$ and $1.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2k & =1 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." 13194139534070 true] [17592186059475 1100 "Calculate $2 {A} + \\dfrac{1}{2} {B}$, where\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${B}=\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        0 & 2 \\\n        4 & 2\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n.$" 13194139534070 true] [17592186059475 1100 "Calculate $2 {A} + \\dfrac{1}{2} {B}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${B}= \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {0 & 2 \\ 4 & 2} \\right\\rbrack$." 13194139534070 false] [17592186059475 1145 "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $2$ and each entry of $B$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2A + \\frac{1}{2}B &= 2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\cdot 1 & 2 \\cdot 5 \\\\ 2 \\cdot 1 & 2 \\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 + 0 & 10 + 1 \\\\ 2 + 2 & 4 + 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534070 false] [17592186059475 1145 "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $2$ and each entry of $B$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A+\\frac{1}{2}B & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0 & 10+1 \\\\ 2+2 & 4+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534070 true] [17592186059665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276532 13194139534070 true] [17592186059665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276546 13194139534070 true] [17592186059665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276555 13194139534070 true] [17592186059665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276565 13194139534070 true] [17592186059665 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276618 13194139